        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 6:41PM CDT by NWS Norman OK</headline>
        <description>At 641 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 4
miles southwest of Tuttle, moving northeast at 40 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Oklahoma City, western Norman, Moore, Midwest City, Del City,
Newcastle, Mustang, Tuttle, Minco, Valley Brook, Bridge Creek, Tinker
Air Force Base, Stanley Draper Lake, Forest Park, Smith Village, The
Capitol, The Fairgrounds, and Will Rogers Airport.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
